.TH LSBLK 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
lsblk \- list block devices and their partitions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lsblk
.SH DESCRIPTION
List every block device under
.B /sys/block
(Linux) with its size and whether it's read-only, followed by its
partitions if any. A summary, not a full replica of the real
.BR lsblk (1)
-- filesystem type, UUID, and mountpoint aren't covered, since
identifying a filesystem means parsing its own superblock format,
which
.BR libblkid
does and this doesn't yet.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if
.B /sys/block
couldn't be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
